Pueblo Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2323 UTC Saturday, August  9, 2025



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z MONDAY/...

Issued at 522 PM MDT Sat Aug 9 2025

Thunderstorms could impact KCOS and KPUB this evening into the 

overnight hours with hail possible at the KCOS terminal through 04Z. 

KPUB has a lower chance for hail, so will maintain -TSRA for now. 

TSRA will percolate along the mountains and plains through the 

overnight hours though chances for storms at the terminals decreases 

after 06z.  VFR cloudiness will linger through the overnight hours 

before clearing Sunday morning.  Another round of -TSRA could impact 

the terminals after 20-21z which could be strong to severe, though 

odds look lower on Sunday.  

KALS will see a window of breezy winds early this evening before 

winds decrease after sundown. VFR cloudiness will linger overnight 

and there is a better chance for -TSRA across the San Luis Valley 

Sunday afternoon.  Odds for this to impact the terminal looks too 

low at this point for a prob30 group in the TAF, but this will 

continue to be assessed for the 06z TAF issuance. -KT





