AFDLMK



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Louisville KY

852 PM EDT Sat Aug 9 2025



.KEY MESSAGES...



* Mostly dry conditions through the weekend, with daily high 

  temperatures in the upper 80s to low 90s through next week.



* Shower and storm chances increase again early next week as cold 

  front approaches the region. Severe weather chances are unlikely.



&&



.UPDATE...

Issued at 851 PM EDT Sat Aug 9 2025



A few isolated showers remain on radar at this hour and will 

continue to dissipate as the sun sets. The remainder of the night 

will feature clear skies and light winds. Some patchy fog 

development is possible in areas that received rain this afternoon. 

Given the isolated-scattered showers from this afternoon and mostly 

a persistence forecast for tomorrow, have introduced some isolated 

PoPs for showers for Sunday afternoon.



&&



.SHORT TERM /THROUGH SUNDAY/...

Issued at 311 PM EDT Sat Aug 9 2025



The axis of an upper ridge now sits over the Lower Ohio Valley 

while to our east, a surface high remains centered off the New 

England coast, and to our west, a surface low sits over southwest 

Kansas. This is keeping our winds light and generally out of the 

south, but some variability has had winds ranging from the southwest 

to southeast throughout southern Indiana and central Kentucky. 

Scattered cumulus is currently covering the CWA, but mid-level 

subsidence has limited convection from developing. Convection 

through the rest of the day isn't out of the question, but 

instability is limited between the high LCLs and mid-level inversion 

of the subsidence, so any convection would be really limited. 



Tonight, the cumulus will dissipate as winds ease to near calm.

Temperatures will dip into the upper 60s to low 70s.  



Tomorrow, the upper ridge will remain over us, but will continue 

moving off to the east as an upper ridge advances towards the 

Midwest through the Northern Plains. Most of the precipitation with 

the trough and co-located front will remain to our northwest. It's 

not out of the question that we could see some isolated pulse 

convection, but the mid-level subsidence will remain, limiting 

potential for development. Mostly sunny skies will lead to highs in 

the low 90s with a few spots remaining in the upper 80s.



&&



.LONG TERM /SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...

Issued at 311 PM EDT Sat Aug 9 2025



==== Sunday Night =====



The upper ridging over the region will shift off to the east in the 

overnight hours. This will lead to another clear and calm night with 

light winds and near normal temperatures. 





===== Monday through Thursday =====



Troughing will overspread the upper Midwest and Gulf moisture will 

increase dew points and PWATs over the lower Ohio Valley next week. 

Monday, scattered showers and storms will likely develop in the 

afternoon over southern Kentucky. Tuesday-Friday, scattered showers 

and storms will become area wide each afternoon. Wednesday 

afternoon, the trough will swing through the Ohio Valley bringing a 

cold front south. This will bring some weak shear to modest CAPE and 

PWATs around 2.0 inches. Could see some stronger storms Wednesday 

afternoon and evening that could bring some gusty winds, heavy 

rainfall, and frequent lightning. At this time, severe storms are 

unlikely.



Temperatures during this time will be in the upper 80s and low 90s 

for highs and low to mid 70s for lows. 





===== Friday and Saturday =====



The trough will push through the region Thursday night, allowing 

ridging to move over the region. The surface front over the region 

will likely push northeast as a warm front. Could see decreased PoPs 

on Friday and Saturday with more isolated chances. With continued 

moisture into the region, increased heights due to ridging, and 

scattered clouds, could see heat indices near 100 in the afternoon. 



Bust potential for this forecast is another trough sweeping through 

the Great Lakes. If this feature extends southward, this could bring 

a front south into the region over the weekend and increase chances 

for showers and storms.



&&



.AVIATION /18Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z TUESDAY/...

Issued at 656 PM EDT Sat Aug 9 2025



A few showers are present on radar at this hour and VCSH is 

mentioned at HNB and LEX for the next few hours. Once the sun sets, 

these showers will dissipate. The remainder of the overnight will 

feature clear skies and light winds. In the morning, winds will pick 

up but remain light. An afternoon Cu field will develop similar to 

the previous days. In the late afternoon, isolated showers will be 

possible.



&&



.LMK WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

KY...None.

IN...None.



&&



$$



UPDATE...SRW

SHORT TERM...KDW

LONG TERM...SRW

AVIATION...SRW



