503

FXUS64 KJAN 100056 AAA

AFDJAN



Area Forecast Discussion...UPDATED

National Weather Service Jackson MS

756 PM CDT Sat Aug 9 2025



...New MESOSCALE UPDATE, AVIATION...



.MESOSCALE UPDATE...

Issued at 748 PM CDT Sat Aug 9 2025



An isolated shower can't entirely be ruled out early this evening,

but the loss of daytime heating is ending rain chances for the

forecast area. Weather elements were updated through the daytime

tomorrow, and only relatively minor adjustments were made. POPs

were increased slightly with latest guidance, but still in mostly

the 20-40% chance range for mostly Interstate 20 and southward by

afternoon. A few hot spots along the more humid river valleys

could see heat index values approach 105 degrees, but no need for

a Heat Advisory at this time. /NF/



&&



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 149 PM CDT Sat Aug 9 2025



Through Next Week...



The "limited" risk for heat stress concerns across the western 

portion of the area continues into next week as temperatures and 

deep layer moisture is returning to near/slightly above 

climatological normals. Heat indices in these area could approach 

105 F into next week. Weakness in the upper ridge as evidenced by an 

upper low shifting westward in the Gulf will continue to yield to 

rising heights locally, supporting the warming trend. Early 

indications suggest the risk area/severity may grow as we approach 

late week and trends will be monitored in that regard. Increases in 

moisture and temperatures will help support increasing rain and 

storm chances each afternoon/evening, particularly for tomorrow and 

into next week. Otherwise, little change in the overall pattern is 

anticipated over the next week.



Tropical expectations remain similar to as discussed yesterday and 

since that time a robust tropical wave has emerged off of Africa, as 

is often the case in August. The NHC designates this feature with a 

40% chance of developments over the next seven days.  Guidance 

spread remains large and thus the wave will just bear watching over 

the next week or so as could be expected this time of year. /86/ 



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 748 PM CDT Sat Aug 9 2025



VFR conditions should prevail at the TAF sites with winds 

generally out of the east at 10 kts or less. /NF/



