Hazardous Weather Outlook

National Weather Service Quad Cities IA IL

238 PM CDT Sun Aug 10 2025



IAZ040>042-051>054-063>068-076>078-087>089-098-099-ILZ001-002-007-

009-015>018-024>026-034-035-MOZ009-010-111945-

Buchanan-Delaware-Dubuque-Benton-Linn-Jones-Jackson-Iowa-Johnson-

Cedar-Clinton-Muscatine-Scott-Keokuk-Washington-Louisa-Jefferson-

Henry IA-Des Moines-Van Buren-Lee-Jo Daviess-Stephenson-Carroll-

Whiteside-Rock Island-Henry IL-Bureau-Putnam-Mercer-Henderson-

Warren-Hancock-McDonough-Scotland-Clark-

238 PM CDT Sun Aug 10 2025



This Hazardous Weather Outlook is for portions of north central

Illinois...northwest Illinois...west central Illinois...east

central Iowa...northeast Iowa...southeast Iowa and northeast

Missouri.



.DAY ONE...THIS AFTERNOON AND TONIGHT



Another round of scattered thunderstorms is forecast this 

afternoon and tonight. A very humid air mass remains in place 

ahead of a cool front and will be capable of hourly rainfall rates

between 1 to 3 inches per hour with the strongest storms. The 

heavy rain may lead to areas of flash flooding and could lead to 

new flooding on area rivers. A Flood Watch remains in effect until

7PM for most of eastern Iowa and northwest Illinois.



Also, the Storm Prediction Center has a Marginal Risk for severe 

storms, with the primary threat damaging winds mainly east of the 

Mississippi River.



.DAYS TWO THROUGH SEVEN...MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY



Occasional rounds of showers and thunderstorms are possible 

through Tuesday morning. Additional heavy rainfall and flash 

flooding are the primary concerns.



.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...



Spotter activation may be needed this afternoon and tonight.



$$



Huyck/WFO Duluth



