Spot Forecast for Adobe Mtn...NDF

National Weather Service Elko NV

418 PM PDT Mon Aug 11 2025



Forecast is based on forecast start time of 1800 PDT on August 11. 

If conditions become unrepresentative, contact the National Weather

Service.



Please contact National Weather Service Elko if you have questions

or concerns with this forecast.



...HEAT ADVISORY IN EFFECT FROM 11 AM TO 8 PM PDT TUESDAY...



.DISCUSSION...Daytime high temperatures will be around five 

degrees warmer than normal Tuesday and Wednesday. Otherwise 

occasional afternoon wind gusts between 20 and 25 mph expected 

Tuesday, slightly stronger Wednesday, up to 30 mph. Slightly 

better instability Tuesday afternoon produces cumulus buildups. 

Enough instability anticipated Wednesday for isolated dry 

thunderstorms in the afternoon and evening. Storm coverage of the 

area looks to be around 15% or less. 



.TONIGHT...



Sky/weather.........Mostly clear (5-15 percent). 

Min temperature.....Around 59. 

Max humidity........34 percent. 

Wind (20 ft)........ 

 Slope/valley.......North winds 5 to 12 mph. 

CWR.................0 percent. 

Mixing height.......0 ft AGL. 

Transport winds.....North around 8 mph. 



.TUESDAY...



Sky/weather.........Mostly sunny (10-20 percent). 

Max temperature.....Around 88. 

Min humidity........13 percent. 

Wind (20 ft)........ 

 Slope/valley.......West winds 5 to 12 mph. 

CWR.................0 percent. 

Mixing height.......5000 ft AGL increasing to 12600 ft AGL late in 

                    the morning. 

Transport winds.....Northwest around 10 mph. 



.TUESDAY NIGHT...



Sky/weather.........Mostly clear (15-25 percent). 

Min temperature.....Around 63. 

Max humidity........28 percent. 

Wind (20 ft)........ 

 Slope/valley.......Northwest winds 5 to 10 mph. 

CWR.................0 percent. 

Mixing height.......12400 ft AGL decreasing to 0 ft AGL early in 

                    the evening. 

Transport winds.....Northwest around 8 mph. 



.WEDNESDAY...



Sky/weather.........Partly cloudy (20-30 percent). Isolated dry

                    Thunderstorms in the afternoon. 

Max temperature.....Around 89. 

Min humidity........14 percent. 

Wind (20 ft)........ 

 Slope/valley.......Light winds becoming west 10 to 16 mph in the 

                    afternoon. 

CWR.................5 percent. 

Mixing height.......100 ft AGL increasing to 12600 ft AGL late in 

                    the morning. 

Transport winds.....West around 14 mph. 



