FWFAFG



Fire Weather Planning Forecast for Interior Alaska

National Weather Service Fairbanks AK

325 PM AKDT Mon Aug 11 2025



.DISCUSSION...

Showery conditions in the far Eastern Interior have mostly ended.

Skies attempt to clear in the Interior although a stubborn layer 

of lower clouds persists across much of the Tanana Valley. Cooler 

temperatures today will give way to highs in the upper 60s to 

lower 70s Tuesday and Wednesday. Minimum RHs drop into the 30s and

40s for most Interior Valleys Tuesday and Wednesday. Generally 

clear skies with no rain expected east of Tanana through Tuesday. 

A low over the West Coast will bring strong a brief period of 

gusty southerly winds Tuesday night to the Alaska Range passes and

over ridgetops. The Upper Tanana Valley will remain the driest 

with minimum RHs in the low 30s to upper 20s Tuesday and 

Wednesday.



The low over the West Coast moves east Wednesday bringing 

increasing cloud cover and rain chances from the east. 

Temperatures cool Thursday and Friday with the rain and cooler 

temperatures stay through the weekend.



