Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Paducah KY

627 PM CDT Mon Aug 11 2025



.KEY MESSAGES...



- Typical summer-time heat and humidity will continue through

  the next 7 days. Daily highs will primarily be in the low 90s

  through Thursday, and may push the mid 90s by the weekend. 



- Chances for showers and storms return this week with the

  highest chances for scattered showers and storms Tuesday into

  Thursday, with lesser chances late in the week and into the

  weekend. 



- Heat index readings will make it "feel like" 95 to 100 degrees

  each day through Thursday. These readings may rise above 100

  and close to 105 in some areas Friday through next weekend.



&&



.UPDATE...

Issued at 627 PM CDT Mon Aug 11 2025



Updated the aviation section for the 00Z TAF issuance. 



&&



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 239 PM CDT Mon Aug 11 2025



Upper level ridging will become centered over the southeast U.S. 

this week with broad troughing, now centered across the central 

plains, moving eastward into the Great Lakes. High pressure at 

the surface off the east coast will allow deeper moisture to 

push in from the Gulf this week. Increasing moisture will work 

with a weak front to produce scattered showers and storms across

the region Tuesday into Thursday. Highest chances will likely 

be Tuesday into Wednesday when the boundary will be closer to 

the region. 



Upper level heights increase later this week and into the weekend 

associated with a building ridge across the southern plains. Weak 

impulses aloft will still present isolated chances of storms during 

the period. Temperatures will remain in the lower 90s for much of the 

week with lows generally in the lower 70s. Hotter temperatures 

look to occur over the weekend associated with building heights 

aloft with highs in the mid 90's. Increasing humidity will occur

through the week with heat indices in the upper 90s to near 

100. Values closer to 105 degrees appear possible over the 

weekend.



&&



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z WEDNESDAY/...

Issued at 627 PM CDT Mon Aug 11 2025



Light winds and VFR cigs are expected through the TAF period.

Showers and a few storms may develop in Northwest Tennessee this

evening and progress northward into far SE Missouri and far SW 

Kentucky. Vsby reductions may occur overnight at KCGI, 

especially if it rains this evening. Tomorrow, isolated to 

scattered showers/thunderstorms develop late in the TAF period, 

mainly in the northwestern and eastern portions of the forecast 

area.



&&



.PAH WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

IL...None.

MO...None.

IN...None.

KY...None.



&&



$$



UPDATE...ATL

DISCUSSION...AD

AVIATION...ATL



