662

SXUS43 KFGF 112331

RECFGF



Recreation Forecast

National Weather Service Grand Forks ND

631 PM CDT Mon Aug 11 2025



Here are the Recreation Area Forecasts...



Wave height forecasts represent the average of the highest 33% of

waves that occur in a given period. Since the significant wave

height is an average of the largest waves, mariners should be

aware that many individual waves will be higher. 



For Devils Lake...



.TONIGHT...West winds 10 to 20 mph. Waves 1 to 2 feet. Chance of

showers and slight chance of thunderstorms in the evening. Mostly

cloudy in the evening then clearing. Lows in the upper 50s. 

.TUESDAY...Breezy. Northwest winds 15 to 25 mph. Waves 1 to

2 feet. Areas of smoke until late afternoon. Sunny. Highs in the

70s. 

.TUESDAY NIGHT...Northwest winds 10 to 15 mph early in the

evening becoming light, then becoming southeast around 10 mph

early in the morning. Waves 1 foot or less. Mostly clear. Lows in

the mid 50s. 





For the Upper and Lower Red Lakes...



.TONIGHT...West winds 10 to 20 mph. Waves 1 to 2 feet. Areas of

smoke early in the evening. Showers likely and chance of

thunderstorms until early morning. Mostly cloudy. Lows around 60.

.TUESDAY...Northwest winds 10 to 20 mph. Waves 2 to 4 feet.

Slight chance of showers in the morning. Areas of smoke in the

late morning and afternoon. Mostly sunny. Highs 65 to 75. 

.TUESDAY NIGHT...Northwest winds 10 to 15 mph until early morning

becoming light. Waves 1 foot or less. Areas of smoke early in the

evening. Partly cloudy. Lows in the mid 50s. 





For Lake of the Woods...



.TONIGHT...Breezy. West winds 15 to 25 mph. Waves 1 to 3 feet.

Areas of smoke early in the evening. Showers likely early in the

evening. Chance of thunderstorms through the night. Chance of

showers early in the morning. Mostly cloudy. Lows in the upper

50s. 

.TUESDAY...Breezy. Northwest winds 15 to 25 mph. Waves 3 to

5 feet. Areas of smoke in the morning. Areas of smoke late in the

afternoon. Chance of thunderstorms through the day. Chance of

showers in the late morning and early afternoon. Slight chance of

thunderstorms early in the afternoon. Mostly sunny. Highs in the

60s. 

.TUESDAY NIGHT...Northwest winds 10 to 20 mph. Waves 1 to 3 feet.

Partly cloudy. Lows in the mid 50s. 





