Fire Weather Planning Forecast for Western Alaska

National Weather Service Fairbanks AK

339 PM AKDT Mon Aug 11 2025



.DISCUSSION...

A coastal storm is bringing heavy rain to the West Coast and 

Western Interior through Wednesday. Southerly winds increase as 

well, especially along the coast and high surf is expected from 

the Seward Peninsula south. The Western Interior is expected to 

see between 0.5 to 2 inches of rain for the event, increasing 

further west in each zone. Elevated terrain in the Seward 

Peninsula and Western Brooks Range will see more with 2 to 4 

inches possible. Rivers and streams will see notable rises in 

water levels. Temperatures in the mid 50s to low 60s expected 

Tuesday and Wednesday cool slightly into the low to mid 50s 

Thursday. Minimum RHs increase today with the incoming rain and 

stay above 60 for most of the week.



