National Weather Service Anchorage AK

341 PM AKDT Mon Aug 11 2025



Offshore Waters Forecast for the Bering Sea



Wind forecasts reflect the predominant speed and direction

expected. Sea forecasts represent an average of the highest

one-third of the combined wind wave and swell height.



PKZ499-121500-

341 PM AKDT Mon Aug 11 2025

.SYNOPSIS FOR CENTRAL BERING SEA...



A front associated with a 993 mb low at 59N 179W sweeps across the 

eastern Bering through Tue. The low crosses Saint Lawrence Island 

before dissipating over Norton Sound by Wed morning. A 1003 mb low at

50N 177W moves to 55N 163W at 1010 mb by Tue afternoon. Another 1006

mb low moves to 50N 178W Wed morning.



