Coastal Waters Forecast

National Weather Service Anchorage Alaska

342 PM AKDT Mon Aug 11 2025



Coastal Waters Forecast for Southwest Alaska+Bristol Bay+The

Alaska Peninsula Waters and the Aleutian Islands up to 100 nm out.



Wind forecasts reflect the predominant speed and direction

expected. Sea forecasts represent an average of the highest

one-third of the combined wind wave and swell height.



PKZ199-121245-

342 PM AKDT Mon Aug 11 2025

.SYNOPSIS FOR SOUTHWEST ALASKA+BRISTOL BAY+THE ALASKA

PENINSULA WATERS AND THE ALEUTIAN ISLANDS...



A front associated with a 993 mb low 190 nm SW of Saint Lawrence 

Island sweeps across the eastern Bering through Tue. The low crosses 

Saint Lawrence Island before dissipating over Norton Sound Wed 

morning. A 1003 mb low 110 nm S of Tanaga Island moves over False 

Pass at 1010 mb Tue afternoon. Another 1006 mb low moves to 90 nm S 

of Amchitka Wed morning.



