FIRE WEATHER PLANNING FORECAST FOR SOUTHWEST ALASKA

NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE ANCHORAGE AK

343 PM AKDT Mon Aug 11 2025



.DISCUSSION...



A frontal system over the eastern Bering Sea will track to the

Southwest coast Tuesday, then weaken as it pushes inland on 

Wednesday. Rain and gusty southerly winds will spread from west 

to east out ahead of the front. This will lead to wet conditions

and marginally cooler temperatures the next couple days. 





