Gusty winds of 20 to 30 kts will continue for SW Colorado sites

with occasionally breezy winds to 20kts elsewhere until sunset

when winds decouple and become light and terrain driven. Smoke

from nearby wildfires is drifting to the south and southwest,

which will impact visibilities at KRIL, KGJT, KASE and

potentially KDRO this evening and overnight. VFR conditions are

expected to prevail regardless with occasionally breezy

westerly winds Tuesday afternoon.





