Albuquerque Aviation Discussion

Issued at 1925 UTC Monday, August 11, 2025



.AVIATION...

(18Z TAFS)

Issued at 122 PM MDT Mon Aug 11 2025

Scattered to numerous thunderstorms are likely this afternoon and 

evening, mainly along and east of the central mountain chain. Storms 

have a marginal chance of becoming severe with damaging winds and 

large hail. Storms are likely to progress across eastern NM after 

00z, moving east-southeast, and many, if not all, eastern NM 

terminals have a risk of being affected. In central NM, outflow 

boundaries from eastern storms will create a gusty gap wind at KSAF 

and more so at KABQ. Current forecast wind speeds at KABQ peak right 

around 35kts near and after 03z, so an AWW may be needed. Isolated 

to scattered storms may continue overnight, mainly across eastern 

NM, but there is low confidence of any impacts to terminals. 



